1
00:00:09,440 --> 00:00:12,920
Make it bright, then try walking away.

2
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:28,420
Like someone calling out to you,
the day after the rain.

3
00:00:29,880 --> 00:00:35,300
Walking while looking back,
led along by Mom's hand.

4
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:42,340
Hey, that strange feeling I had back then.

5
00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:47,700
So, on the tiles of the arcade street,

6
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:53,480
I walked only on the black ones.

7
00:00:55,820 --> 00:01:01,780
Everyone was a child once,
but everyone forgets.

8
00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:09,100
Even the politicians with their pompous faces,
and the aunties with blue eyeshadow.

9
00:01:09,580 --> 00:01:14,660
Come on, turn at that corner.

10
00:01:15,660 --> 00:01:19,880
You can meet everyone, everyone.

11
00:01:22,080 --> 00:01:27,780
Over there is Kame-ari
surely there's Kame-ari.

12
00:01:27,780 --> 00:01:32,960
Everyone, come on over to our town.

13
00:01:33,920 --> 00:01:34,540
Thank you.

14
00:01:39,420 --> 00:01:42,440
Jet

15
00:01:43,020 --> 00:01:44,340
Ippon!

16
00:01:44,340 --> 00:01:46,900
Ippon!

17
00:01:46,900 --> 00:01:49,080
Ippon!

18
00:01:49,080 --> 00:01:51,220
Ippon!

19
00:01:51,220 --> 00:01:56,880
Ippon!

20
00:01:57,780 --> 00:02:00,620
We did it! Kameari Kōen-mae Police Box team!

21
00:02:00,640 --> 00:02:02,500
We've been chosen as Katsushika
Precinct's representatives!

22
00:02:02,840 --> 00:02:03,800
We did it! We did it!

23
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:05,480
Whoo!

24
00:02:05,820 --> 00:02:09,300
Wasshan! Wasshan! Wasshan!

25
00:02:12,740 --> 00:02:14,860
Kameari Kōen-mae Police Box

26
00:02:22,360 --> 00:02:25,440
My sword is one-hearted,
no foe stands before me.

27
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:31,900
Ugh! It's heavy!

28
00:02:32,280 --> 00:02:34,580
I won't let this grudge go unavenged!

29
00:02:35,320 --> 00:02:38,060
Just you wait,
Kameari Kōen-mae Prime Minister!

30
00:02:39,680 --> 00:02:41,620
Kendo, straight strike!

31
00:02:51,520 --> 00:02:52,500
Die!

32
00:02:52,640 --> 00:02:54,500
Ow ow!

33
00:02:54,780 --> 00:02:57,560
S-senpai, that's a foul!

34
00:02:58,780 --> 00:03:02,440
Good for the real thing The
customers are so annoying.

35
00:03:02,840 --> 00:03:04,200
Baramon!

36
00:03:04,200 --> 00:03:08,660
Chief, what are you doing?
Striking the same spot twice is underhanded!

37
00:03:08,660 --> 00:03:13,560
Who's being underhanded? Going for the shins!
Is there such a messed-up kind of kendo?

38
00:03:13,560 --> 00:03:16,080
Well, if you're facing off with real swords,
you see...

39
00:03:16,660 --> 00:03:19,600
Just winning at any cost is heterodox,
evil swordsmanship!

40
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:23,140
Come, Ryotsu!
I'll knock that attitude straight into you.

41
00:03:23,980 --> 00:03:26,640
Look, Chief Ohara and
Ryotsu are about to go at it!

42
00:03:26,640 --> 00:03:29,600
Even Ryotsu can't beat Chief Ohara, can he?

43
00:03:30,640 --> 00:03:32,640
Come at me from anywhere.

44
00:03:33,560 --> 00:03:36,860
Alright, let's give it a shot, then.

45
00:03:48,620 --> 00:03:51,360
Damn it, there's no opening anywhere!

46
00:03:52,940 --> 00:03:54,320
Chiyoko Shimakura!

47
00:03:55,080 --> 00:03:55,880
Now!

48
00:03:57,040 --> 00:03:57,740
Here!

49
00:04:04,720 --> 00:04:08,160
Listen, Ryotsu.
Kendo is a battle against yourself.

50
00:04:08,260 --> 00:04:10,097
If you always keep a calm mind,

51
00:04:10,147 --> 00:04:12,760
you'll never lose to a
wicked sword like yours.

52
00:04:12,920 --> 00:04:14,360
As expected of Chief Ohara.

53
00:04:14,560 --> 00:04:15,120
That's amazing.

54
00:04:15,460 --> 00:04:16,960
That's very convincing.

55
00:04:17,380 --> 00:04:20,580
Chief Ohara's sword really is
the best in Katsushika Precinct.

56
00:04:20,900 --> 00:04:23,640
No, no, Ohara. Well done, well done.

57
00:04:23,640 --> 00:04:26,480
Keep it up and do well in
the main tournament too.

58
00:04:26,480 --> 00:04:28,500
I'll do my best.

59
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:31,620
If we achieve back-to-back
wins like last year,

60
00:04:31,620 --> 00:04:33,420
I'll be able to hold my head
high among the other chiefs,

61
00:04:33,420 --> 00:04:34,760
I'll be so proud, you know.

62
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:36,860
Damn it.

63
00:04:36,860 --> 00:04:38,440
That Chief!

64
00:04:43,780 --> 00:04:45,400
He comes in like this, then like that.

65
00:04:45,400 --> 00:04:46,760
If I do this,

66
00:04:47,380 --> 00:04:48,260
Yes!

67
00:04:48,260 --> 00:04:49,920
I've found his weakness!

68
00:04:50,380 --> 00:04:52,440
What are you doing, senpai?

69
00:04:53,640 --> 00:04:56,820
A new game?
Geez, you never get tired of these, do you?

70
00:04:57,860 --> 00:05:00,720
Wrong! This is a kendo simulation.

71
00:05:00,720 --> 00:05:02,240
This is...

72
00:05:02,240 --> 00:05:06,000
I get it! You want to beat our
rivals at Shibamata Station, right?

73
00:05:07,160 --> 00:05:07,560
No.

74
00:05:08,960 --> 00:05:10,940
It's to beat the Chief!

75
00:05:11,520 --> 00:05:13,320
The Chief?

76
00:05:13,980 --> 00:05:18,500
That's right! I've input all of the
Chief's movements from his past matches.

77
00:05:18,500 --> 00:05:21,400
With this, I'll know all of
the Chief's attack patterns.

78
00:05:21,400 --> 00:05:22,200
Got it?

79
00:05:23,640 --> 00:05:26,420
This is the Chief, and this is me.

80
00:05:27,040 --> 00:05:30,140
Say I charge straight at him,

81
00:05:30,140 --> 00:05:34,980
and the Chief dodges to
the left with an 80% chance.

82
00:05:34,980 --> 00:05:37,560
I'll immediately aim for his right tsuba.

83
00:05:37,560 --> 00:05:39,920
Senpai's men is wide open.

84
00:05:39,920 --> 00:05:44,820
But at that moment, the Chief's counterattack has only two patterns:
kote or dō.

85
00:05:44,820 --> 00:05:46,760
He'd never go for men.

86
00:05:48,240 --> 00:05:52,400
So if I step in one beat
early like this and strike dō,

87
00:05:54,400 --> 00:05:56,380
how about that? I win.

88
00:05:56,380 --> 00:05:58,960
Wow, you really studied it well, Ryo-san.

89
00:05:59,480 --> 00:06:03,220
But winning against the Chief, who's on our own team,
doesn't really count for anything, does it?

90
00:06:03,220 --> 00:06:06,020
You two wouldn't understand.

91
00:06:06,020 --> 00:06:08,400
This is a matter of a man's pride.

92
00:06:08,400 --> 00:06:09,760
Just watch, Chief.

93
00:06:09,760 --> 00:06:10,600
Orie.

94
00:06:30,520 --> 00:06:32,720
Alright then, here I come, Chief!

95
00:06:32,720 --> 00:06:37,760
I won't lose to the sword of
someone with a twisted heart like you.

96
00:06:37,760 --> 00:06:41,060
Just watch, you'll see.

97
00:06:44,500 --> 00:06:46,140
Just as the simulation predicted.

98
00:06:47,520 --> 00:06:48,480
Now!

99
00:06:49,280 --> 00:06:49,760
Aaaaah!

100
00:06:49,760 --> 00:06:53,700
Aaaaah! Ippon!

101
00:06:55,020 --> 00:07:01,880
Yes! The Chief lost!
What a cheap, mass-produced ippon win!

102
00:07:02,740 --> 00:07:10,940
I lost? Heh, sorry,
the one with the twisted heart got the win.

103
00:07:10,940 --> 00:07:14,360
M-my sword lost to Ryotsu!

104
00:07:15,060 --> 00:07:18,240
You still need more training, Chief.

105
00:07:18,240 --> 00:07:20,320
There's always someone better than you.

106
00:07:23,340 --> 00:07:25,860
What was all that training for?

107
00:07:26,800 --> 00:07:28,740
That Chief...

108
00:07:28,740 --> 00:07:33,480
Senpai analyzed the Chief's movement patterns using a computer,
you know.

109
00:07:33,480 --> 00:07:34,300
What did you say?

110
00:07:34,300 --> 00:07:38,460
The Chief's so stubborn,
he can only make the same moves.

111
00:07:38,460 --> 00:07:40,400
That was a solid strategy, too.

112
00:07:42,480 --> 00:07:44,360
Either way, a loss is a loss.

113
00:07:44,360 --> 00:07:46,560
I simply didn't train enough.

114
00:07:46,560 --> 00:07:48,400
I'll start over from scratch.

115
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:50,020
Excuse me.

116
00:07:51,580 --> 00:07:52,720
Ohara-kun.

117
00:07:52,720 --> 00:07:54,000
Ohara-kun.

118
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:56,780
You'll be taking part in the next kendo tournament,
won't you?

119
00:07:56,780 --> 00:07:58,560
Without you, it just wouldn't be the same.

120
00:08:00,760 --> 00:08:01,580
Chief,

121
00:08:01,580 --> 00:08:03,540
with you here, we'll be fine!

122
00:08:03,540 --> 00:08:06,740
Following last year,
a second straight win is certain.

123
00:08:07,320 --> 00:08:10,240
But Shibamata station,
which lost to us last year,

124
00:08:10,940 --> 00:08:12,740
is said to have prepared a secret weapon.

125
00:08:12,740 --> 00:08:13,980
A secret weapon?

126
00:08:14,840 --> 00:08:19,140
Rumor has it that Kojiro
Sasaki is competing for them.

127
00:08:19,140 --> 00:08:21,180
Kojiro Sasaki?

128
00:08:21,260 --> 00:08:22,620
You know him, Gei-chan?

129
00:08:22,620 --> 00:08:24,420
Yes, he's famous.

130
00:08:24,420 --> 00:08:27,380
Nakagawa, is he really that strong?

131
00:08:28,120 --> 00:08:32,840
Kojiro Sasaki won the national championships
in both high school and university,

132
00:08:32,840 --> 00:08:35,300
and even became a professional swordsman.
He's a genius.

133
00:08:35,780 --> 00:08:38,680
He's the master of a secret sword
technique called Sparrow Return.

134
00:08:39,100 --> 00:08:40,280
Sparrow Return?

135
00:08:40,940 --> 00:08:42,240
Not Swallow Return?

136
00:08:42,300 --> 00:08:44,340
Yes, it's a terrifying technique.

137
00:08:44,980 --> 00:08:46,780
By the way, here's what his face looks like.

138
00:08:51,600 --> 00:08:53,460
I am Sasaki Kojiro.

139
00:08:53,930 --> 00:08:54,480
What?

140
00:08:55,160 --> 00:08:57,720
Ha ha ha ha ha hamburg!

141
00:08:58,520 --> 00:09:01,660
No wonder you're surprised.
I'm rather handsome, after all.

142
00:09:01,660 --> 00:09:04,240
So this is Sasaki Kojiro?

143
00:09:04,240 --> 00:09:05,740
H-he's a weird one.

144
00:09:05,740 --> 00:09:06,440
and

145
00:09:08,200 --> 00:09:09,840
Don't stand behind me.

146
00:09:10,640 --> 00:09:11,520
Well...

147
00:09:12,940 --> 00:09:14,140
Shibamata Station Chief

148
00:09:14,740 --> 00:09:17,140
You've been standing behind us this whole time,
haven't you?

149
00:09:18,280 --> 00:09:20,600
Hello, hello, Chief Tomita.

150
00:09:20,600 --> 00:09:21,640
Did you see that?

151
00:09:21,640 --> 00:09:24,620
This man is the secret weapon
of our Shibamata Station.

152
00:09:24,620 --> 00:09:26,920
Ha ha ha ha hedgehog!

153
00:09:26,920 --> 00:09:29,040
Something is definitely off.

154
00:09:29,040 --> 00:09:32,040
But why on earth would someone
like that be at Shibamata Station?

155
00:09:33,200 --> 00:09:36,420
So that means we scouted him ourselves,
Shibamata-sho.

156
00:09:36,420 --> 00:09:38,740
What, how dirty!

157
00:09:38,740 --> 00:09:42,080
This year, Shibamata Station
is taking the championship!

158
00:09:42,080 --> 00:10:06,360
Hahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahaha

159
00:10:06,360 --> 00:10:07,720
It must be! Right?

160
00:10:08,260 --> 00:10:09,700
Yeah, right!

161
00:10:09,760 --> 00:10:10,900
Y-yes!

162
00:10:11,500 --> 00:10:13,112
Hmph, you're a lucky one.

163
00:10:13,162 --> 00:10:16,820
Another 3.5 millimeters
forward and you'd have been dead.

164
00:10:16,860 --> 00:10:18,660
Hey! That's too forceful!

165
00:10:18,940 --> 00:10:20,460
What did you just say, you?

166
00:10:20,680 --> 00:10:22,180
But that's totally forced!

167
00:10:22,700 --> 00:10:23,560
Ryo-chan.

168
00:10:24,340 --> 00:10:27,780
I see. You're that eager
to see my Sparrow Return?

169
00:10:27,980 --> 00:10:29,440
I never said that!

170
00:10:29,780 --> 00:10:32,680
But if you see it, you'll die.
Are you still fine with that?

171
00:10:32,940 --> 00:10:35,340
Hmph, fine. Only once, though.

172
00:10:40,580 --> 00:10:41,820
Flies, right?

173
00:10:42,500 --> 00:10:43,360
Whoa!

174
00:10:43,680 --> 00:10:47,920
Jakeru! Suzume! Tsunaishī! Jigonbeikē!

175
00:10:48,440 --> 00:10:49,820
Whoa! So fast!

176
00:10:52,520 --> 00:10:54,580
Whoa! It's a sparrow!

177
00:10:55,840 --> 00:10:58,140
I've gotten into another
pointless negotiation.

178
00:11:00,180 --> 00:11:03,140
Hey, weren't you aiming for that fly?

179
00:11:04,700 --> 00:11:05,340
You...

180
00:11:05,390 --> 00:11:09,300
You've really made me angry now.

181
00:11:09,300 --> 00:11:11,940
You didn't even come close to the fly!

182
00:11:11,940 --> 00:11:15,080
And you call it an evil sword yourself!

183
00:11:15,080 --> 00:11:16,960
Were you born in Hiroshima or something?

184
00:11:16,960 --> 00:11:18,500
Jaken, jaken!

185
00:11:21,500 --> 00:11:22,560
It's a duel!

186
00:11:23,040 --> 00:11:25,220
Duel me on solid ground!

187
00:11:25,800 --> 00:11:27,120
D-duel?

188
00:11:27,120 --> 00:11:34,480
How about we settle it next Saturday?

189
00:11:34,480 --> 00:11:35,460
Taian, the lucky day!

190
00:11:35,460 --> 00:11:38,380
By the way, today's Butsumetsu,
the unluckiest day, so let's not do it.

191
00:11:39,300 --> 00:11:41,680
Challenging someone to a duel and
then going by superstition like that!

192
00:11:41,680 --> 00:11:42,340
I'm going to say it!

193
00:11:43,420 --> 00:11:45,360
They say luck is part of skill, right?

194
00:11:45,820 --> 00:11:47,060
This too is part of strategy.

195
00:11:47,780 --> 00:11:50,760
Listen, the duel will be on Ganryu Island.

196
00:11:51,720 --> 00:11:52,700
Ganryu Island.

197
00:11:53,140 --> 00:11:56,600
The famous duel between Miyamoto
Musashi and Sasaki Kojiro...

198
00:11:56,980 --> 00:12:00,600
...was far off, so it's Ganryu Island,
thirty minutes by train from here.

199
00:12:02,160 --> 00:12:03,460
The time is 9 a.m.

200
00:12:03,460 --> 00:12:05,100
Got it? Farewell!

201
00:12:05,620 --> 00:12:07,180
Hey, don't decide things on your own!

202
00:12:08,320 --> 00:12:11,000
Well, I suppose I should
prepare my victory speech.

203
00:12:12,880 --> 00:12:14,000
Don't stand behind me.

204
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:15,860
I've told you, it's me!

205
00:12:17,800 --> 00:12:19,080
Soft-boiled egg.

206
00:12:19,840 --> 00:12:22,240
These people are strange, aren't they.

207
00:12:22,240 --> 00:12:24,980
It's clear they're idiots.

208
00:12:25,620 --> 00:12:28,600
Now we have to beat Shibamata
Station no matter what.

209
00:12:28,600 --> 00:12:30,800
If we win, I'll give you a special bonus.

210
00:12:31,940 --> 00:12:33,160
Really, Chief?

211
00:12:34,400 --> 00:12:35,860
Yes, I'm counting on you, Ryotsu.

212
00:12:37,180 --> 00:12:41,280
Leave it to me. I'll definitely beat
Shibamata Station and win the tournament.

213
00:12:41,280 --> 00:12:43,760
But what are we going to do about the duel?

214
00:12:43,760 --> 00:12:45,000
That's right, Ryo-chan.

215
00:12:45,560 --> 00:12:48,700
I've got a plan too.

216
00:13:06,540 --> 00:13:10,660
The reason we came to Ganryu Island
a day early is none other than

217
00:13:11,340 --> 00:13:13,760
We can't rely on the Chief, so

218
00:13:14,300 --> 00:13:18,320
to surely win the
Katsushika kendo tournament,

219
00:13:18,700 --> 00:13:20,288
let's make the most of this opportunity.

220
00:13:20,338 --> 00:13:23,980
It's best to take care of him here.

221
00:13:25,340 --> 00:13:27,940
Just watch, Sasaki Kojiro.

222
00:13:51,220 --> 00:13:52,240
You finally came, Ryotsu.

223
00:13:56,360 --> 00:13:57,620
You're late, Ryotsu!

224
00:13:57,620 --> 00:13:59,280
Are you trying to copy Musashi?

225
00:14:01,860 --> 00:14:02,600
Damn it.

226
00:14:02,600 --> 00:14:04,860
I forgot to set my alarm clock.

227
00:14:05,320 --> 00:14:05,960
I'm late!

228
00:14:16,720 --> 00:14:17,200
Late.

229
00:14:17,600 --> 00:14:18,420
You're way too late!

230
00:14:20,320 --> 00:14:21,040
Hey!

231
00:14:21,560 --> 00:14:24,480
Sorry, sorry! I overslept!

232
00:14:24,820 --> 00:14:27,240
Musashi! No, Ryotsu!
I've been waiting for you!

233
00:14:27,720 --> 00:14:29,020
Yaaah!

234
00:14:29,080 --> 00:14:30,560
Wait, Chikuchiku!

235
00:14:30,780 --> 00:14:31,400
Please!

236
00:14:31,820 --> 00:14:33,860
Kojiro, you're beaten!

237
00:14:33,980 --> 00:14:34,420
What?

238
00:14:34,820 --> 00:14:35,520
Whoa, aah!

239
00:14:37,360 --> 00:14:38,500
W-what is this?

240
00:14:39,160 --> 00:14:41,797
It's the pitfall I set up yesterday.

241
00:14:41,847 --> 00:14:43,340
You fell right into it.

242
00:14:43,680 --> 00:14:45,560
Wow, how cowardly!

243
00:14:46,040 --> 00:14:48,160
Cowardly, my ass,
but this is the final blow!

244
00:14:51,340 --> 00:14:53,880
What? Why is there a pit here?

245
00:14:55,560 --> 00:14:59,780
Hatomugi-chan, I set traps too, you know.

246
00:14:59,780 --> 00:15:01,220
That's dirty, Hikiyamaro!

247
00:15:01,860 --> 00:15:05,420
This is also part of strategy.
There are no rules in a duel.

248
00:15:05,420 --> 00:15:08,120
It's you who should be prepared.

249
00:15:08,120 --> 00:15:09,300
No way I'll let that happen.

250
00:15:14,960 --> 00:15:16,300
What? What do I do?

251
00:15:21,620 --> 00:15:23,580
What a guy.

252
00:15:23,580 --> 00:15:24,780
It's you.

253
00:15:27,320 --> 00:15:33,500
Chashu.

254
00:15:34,290 --> 00:15:35,240
Crack.

255
00:15:46,740 --> 00:15:48,300
Prepare yourself!

256
00:15:49,960 --> 00:15:50,540
Feint!

257
00:15:50,700 --> 00:15:51,440
Ugh, the claws!

258
00:15:52,120 --> 00:15:53,160
Alright, one point!

259
00:15:53,660 --> 00:15:54,480
Is that so?

260
00:15:55,440 --> 00:15:57,820
I'm wearing shin guards, so I'm fine, right?

261
00:15:58,240 --> 00:16:00,200
Are you a pro baseball catcher or something!

262
00:16:00,640 --> 00:16:01,940
This too is part of the art of war!

263
00:16:02,160 --> 00:16:02,780
Kannon mask!

264
00:16:02,900 --> 00:16:03,660
Soldering iron!

265
00:16:03,860 --> 00:16:05,020
Do-Re-Mi Attract!

266
00:16:05,400 --> 00:16:06,340
Wait! Hey, hey!

267
00:16:06,660 --> 00:16:07,200
Time out!

268
00:16:07,460 --> 00:16:08,160
What about time out?

269
00:16:08,400 --> 00:16:08,880
Ichimoku!

270
00:16:09,200 --> 00:16:10,020
Oboro-zuki!

271
00:16:11,080 --> 00:16:12,140
Gomoku soba!

272
00:16:12,420 --> 00:16:14,180
That's not gomoku soba, you idiot!

273
00:16:14,600 --> 00:16:16,380
I'm not the type to fuss over details.

274
00:16:16,620 --> 00:16:18,780
I'm not the type to
fuss over details either.

275
00:16:19,700 --> 00:16:20,300
Yes!

276
00:16:20,640 --> 00:16:22,040
Crap!

277
00:16:22,060 --> 00:16:23,160
Heh, take that!

278
00:16:23,260 --> 00:16:24,120
Mister, this way!

279
00:16:24,500 --> 00:16:25,720
Damn it! Wait!

280
00:16:28,800 --> 00:16:30,900
You followed me! Right where I wanted you!

281
00:16:31,440 --> 00:16:35,320
Fool! This grove is packed with explosives!

282
00:16:36,100 --> 00:16:38,860
I'll settle this once and for all!

283
00:16:44,220 --> 00:16:47,160
Whoa! We're going to kill him!

284
00:16:55,960 --> 00:16:58,200
Senpai, are you really all right?

285
00:16:58,200 --> 00:17:00,540
It's nothing serious.

286
00:17:01,060 --> 00:17:05,200
But he set explosives in the same spot too!

287
00:17:05,200 --> 00:17:09,420
I hear he's badly hurt
and can't compete, though.

288
00:17:10,100 --> 00:17:13,940
We will now begin the police
station kendo tournament.

289
00:17:30,420 --> 00:17:32,320
You all did well.

290
00:17:32,320 --> 00:17:34,020
The final match is finally here!

291
00:17:34,020 --> 00:17:35,320
Leave it to us.

292
00:17:35,800 --> 00:17:38,840
But the final is against
that Shibamata station, right?

293
00:17:38,840 --> 00:17:42,460
We only won last year because
Chief Ohara was with us.

294
00:17:43,940 --> 00:17:45,040
We've got me, the one who won!

295
00:17:45,040 --> 00:17:46,580
I told you, it's fine!

296
00:17:46,580 --> 00:17:48,460
Count on you, Ryotsu.

297
00:17:48,460 --> 00:17:48,980
Yes.

298
00:17:48,980 --> 00:17:52,020
And don't forget the
station chief's bonus, either.

299
00:17:52,020 --> 00:17:53,260
I know that.

300
00:17:53,260 --> 00:17:56,000
So the Chief didn't come after all

301
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:56,400
Yeah.

302
00:17:57,160 --> 00:17:59,920
We will now begin the final match.

303
00:18:00,560 --> 00:18:01,560
The teams facing off are

304
00:18:01,560 --> 00:18:04,240
last year's runners-up,
the Shibamata Station team,

305
00:18:04,720 --> 00:18:05,900
and last year's champions,

306
00:18:05,900 --> 00:18:07,600
the Katsushika Station team.

307
00:18:08,700 --> 00:18:09,960
Both teams, step forward.

308
00:18:09,960 --> 00:18:10,660
Yes.

309
00:18:12,040 --> 00:18:13,040
Haaah!

310
00:18:14,120 --> 00:18:14,480
This is...!

311
00:18:17,860 --> 00:18:19,920
Why do they all have the same face?

312
00:18:20,100 --> 00:18:21,600
Five Kojiros?

313
00:18:22,980 --> 00:18:25,430
This is the trump card
of our Shibamata style,

314
00:18:25,480 --> 00:18:27,020
the Six Sasakki Brothers!

315
00:18:27,260 --> 00:18:28,960
The eldest, Sasakki Koichiro.

316
00:18:28,960 --> 00:18:31,060
The third son, Sasakki Kosaburo.

317
00:18:31,480 --> 00:18:33,180
The fourth son, Sasakki Koshiro.

318
00:18:33,660 --> 00:18:35,260
The fifth son, Sasakki Kogoro.

319
00:18:35,720 --> 00:18:37,260
The sixth son, Sasakki Korokuro.

320
00:18:37,260 --> 00:18:39,620
Wahhh! Hahaha!

321
00:18:39,620 --> 00:18:43,100
Harmageddon!
And I am the second son, Sasakki Kojiro!

322
00:18:43,540 --> 00:18:45,600
That's all. The Six Sasakki Brothers!

323
00:18:45,900 --> 00:18:47,780
Could they be the Mutsugo brothers?

324
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:49,500
Are you guys Osomatsu-kun?

325
00:18:49,960 --> 00:18:51,140
What do we do, Ryo-san?

326
00:18:51,140 --> 00:18:53,880
Six idiots like that?!

327
00:18:54,100 --> 00:18:56,260
But we have no choice
but to fight now, right?

328
00:18:57,680 --> 00:19:00,820
That's right! What's there to think about?
We've got no choice but to go for it!

329
00:19:04,900 --> 00:19:05,620
Point!

330
00:19:08,500 --> 00:19:14,860
Th-that's fine, right? Ryo-kun, leave it to me.
In return, if we win the championship, a special bonus!

331
00:19:14,860 --> 00:19:21,900
Double for the bridge only, okay? Boy, I've got to work twice as hard,
all by myself, covering for Chief Ohara too, so...

332
00:19:22,480 --> 00:19:28,080
Alright, got it, I'll splurge. That's what I like to hear! Yeah,
two points, two points!

333
00:19:28,840 --> 00:19:29,640
Begin!

334
00:19:29,640 --> 00:19:31,080
Yaaah!

335
00:19:31,420 --> 00:19:32,880
We did it!

336
00:19:33,880 --> 00:19:34,580
Point!

337
00:19:34,740 --> 00:19:35,960
Senior Constable Ryotsu!

338
00:19:36,600 --> 00:19:38,140
Amazing, amazing! Ryo-chan!

339
00:19:38,460 --> 00:19:41,960
When the wind's blowing,
my power is immense!

340
00:19:42,140 --> 00:19:43,480
Hahahaha!

341
00:19:43,520 --> 00:19:44,280
Harahira!

342
00:19:44,560 --> 00:19:46,640
Hey! Don't copy my gag!

343
00:19:46,960 --> 00:19:49,660
Hey! Kogoro! Hurry up and finish him!

344
00:19:49,900 --> 00:19:50,360
Ugh!

345
00:19:51,040 --> 00:19:51,860
Whoa!

346
00:19:52,560 --> 00:19:53,520
Go for it, Ryo-chan!

347
00:19:53,700 --> 00:19:54,280
Ryo-chan!

348
00:19:54,420 --> 00:19:54,880
Senpai!

349
00:19:55,620 --> 00:19:57,040
Meeen!

350
00:20:05,840 --> 00:20:07,100
Amazing! Ryo-chan!

351
00:20:07,320 --> 00:20:08,060
Four in a row!

352
00:20:08,360 --> 00:20:10,020
Only one more to go, senpai!

353
00:20:12,280 --> 00:20:14,760
Still, I'm a bit tired.

354
00:20:14,760 --> 00:20:17,980
But only one more!
One more and it's the special bonus!

355
00:20:19,300 --> 00:20:21,760
Damn! Go get him, big brother!

356
00:20:22,860 --> 00:20:24,700
Leave it to me.

357
00:20:24,700 --> 00:20:25,400
Yeah!

358
00:20:26,080 --> 00:20:28,120
Two swords?! This one is...

359
00:20:29,260 --> 00:20:31,540
You seem pretty tired.

360
00:20:31,540 --> 00:20:34,300
Fusea Killer

361
00:20:34,780 --> 00:20:35,800
Revenge for my brothers.

362
00:20:35,800 --> 00:20:36,540
Begin!

363
00:20:36,540 --> 00:20:37,580
Prepare yourself.

364
00:20:38,960 --> 00:20:41,280
Jacket Double Super Return

365
00:20:47,440 --> 00:20:47,980
Your arm...

366
00:20:48,440 --> 00:20:49,140
There!

367
00:20:54,340 --> 00:20:55,140
He's staggering!

368
00:20:55,140 --> 00:20:56,380
Senpai!

369
00:20:56,380 --> 00:20:59,400
Beef hash!

370
00:20:59,400 --> 00:21:00,720
You did it, big brother!

371
00:21:01,540 --> 00:21:04,240
Damn it! Our bonus!

372
00:21:04,620 --> 00:21:06,500
Next, Captain, step up!

373
00:21:09,440 --> 00:21:12,700
Didn't Chief Ohara wander off somewhere?

374
00:21:13,260 --> 00:21:16,580
So that means the championship is ours.

375
00:21:19,540 --> 00:21:20,420
Wait!

376
00:21:21,240 --> 00:21:23,780
I am the captain of the
Katsushika Station team!

377
00:21:27,320 --> 00:21:28,180
Chief!

378
00:21:28,440 --> 00:21:29,040
Chief!

379
00:21:29,040 --> 00:21:30,900
Ohara-kun

380
00:21:32,580 --> 00:21:33,660
Chief Ohara

381
00:21:36,180 --> 00:21:37,520
Fukujinzuke

382
00:21:37,520 --> 00:21:40,720
How foolish of you to come out just to lose.

383
00:21:41,220 --> 00:21:44,780
No one can defeat this Sasakki Kojiro!

384
00:21:45,420 --> 00:21:46,820
Now, I shall advance!

385
00:21:47,340 --> 00:21:49,240
Then, the captains' match, begin!

386
00:21:59,040 --> 00:22:05,020
Open stance,
a natural posture in the middle guard.

387
00:22:05,020 --> 00:22:12,220
It's suited for both attack and defense. There's no
opening to strike. He must have practiced somewhere already.

388
00:22:12,740 --> 00:22:20,060
I didn't expect the Chief to have improved this much.
Hey, what's wrong, brother? Hurry up and finish him off!

389
00:22:20,060 --> 00:22:20,600
Free!

390
00:22:21,220 --> 00:22:21,580
Men!

391
00:22:21,580 --> 00:22:23,220
Jacket! Double Sparrow Return!

392
00:22:23,440 --> 00:22:24,140
We're going to be hit!

393
00:22:26,140 --> 00:22:26,800
Shoot!

394
00:22:28,940 --> 00:22:30,460
It's the same pattern again!

395
00:22:30,620 --> 00:22:32,000
At this rate, we're going to lose!

396
00:22:32,300 --> 00:22:32,800
Chief!

397
00:22:33,040 --> 00:22:33,420
Chief!

398
00:22:33,960 --> 00:22:34,440
Got it!

399
00:22:35,880 --> 00:22:36,360
Dear!

400
00:22:39,440 --> 00:22:40,920
Florie-kar!

401
00:22:41,520 --> 00:22:43,240
Dear!

402
00:22:43,780 --> 00:22:44,340
Four!

403
00:22:46,400 --> 00:22:47,200
Ippon!

404
00:22:47,400 --> 00:22:48,000
That's it!

405
00:22:48,680 --> 00:22:51,500
We did it! The champion is Katsushika's

406
00:22:53,440 --> 00:22:53,820
representative team!

407
00:22:54,280 --> 00:22:55,040
Chief!

408
00:22:56,300 --> 00:22:58,820
We did it, our championship!

409
00:23:01,940 --> 00:23:05,240
Everyone did their best on my behalf.

410
00:23:05,240 --> 00:23:06,720
What are you talking about?

411
00:23:06,720 --> 00:23:10,500
You're the one who brilliantly
overcame your weakness, Chief.

412
00:23:11,040 --> 00:23:14,420
You got hurt too,
but you pushed through well.

413
00:23:14,420 --> 00:23:18,360
We only won the championship
thanks to you, Chief.

414
00:23:18,360 --> 00:23:19,420
Ohara-kun.

415
00:23:19,420 --> 00:23:21,280
You all did a great job.

416
00:23:21,280 --> 00:23:23,420
You're the pride of Katsushika Station.

417
00:23:23,820 --> 00:23:26,000
Now, the special bonus I promised!

418
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:27,080
Bonus...

419
00:23:27,080 --> 00:23:30,100
No, Station Chief,
I didn't do it for something like that...

420
00:23:30,100 --> 00:23:30,480
Station Chief.

421
00:23:30,480 --> 00:23:33,740
The bonus is over here, this way.

422
00:23:34,400 --> 00:23:35,820
You're hopeless.

423
00:23:35,820 --> 00:23:37,400
We went and lost, didn't we?

424
00:23:37,400 --> 00:23:40,340
Besides, just now everyone said
it was all thanks to the Chief,

425
00:23:40,340 --> 00:23:42,080
and you said it too, didn't you?

426
00:23:42,700 --> 00:23:43,100
No way...

427
00:23:44,700 --> 00:23:46,660
That's not right, Station Chief.

428
00:23:46,660 --> 00:23:49,160
it was also thanks to me that
the Chief overcame his weakness,

429
00:23:49,160 --> 00:23:50,800
it's all because of me.

430
00:23:51,280 --> 00:23:53,800
I worked so hard I got seriously hurt.

431
00:23:53,800 --> 00:23:56,120
You said we don't need the Chief, so

432
00:23:56,120 --> 00:23:58,180
give me my bonus, come on.

433
00:23:58,180 --> 00:23:59,040
Heave-ho, here we go!

434
00:24:01,100 --> 00:24:05,460
I kicked the alarm clock
and stubbed my pinky, ow ow

435
00:24:05,460 --> 00:24:13,740
First I draw on my eyebrows, then it's dance,
dance, dance all the way to the station!

436
00:24:13,740 --> 00:24:19,340
Packed commuter train, a nap on Dad's back.

437
00:24:22,280 --> 00:24:25,680
Hard work and hardship,
you're absolutely right.

438
00:24:26,900 --> 00:24:30,520
Holding a baguette in one hand,
looking all posh.

439
00:24:30,520 --> 00:24:33,340
Beef bowl, special, extra sauce.

440
00:24:33,340 --> 00:24:36,600
The irritation from endless overtime,

441
00:24:36,600 --> 00:24:40,200
irritation, all cleared away in a flash.

442
00:24:43,540 --> 00:24:46,080
Every day is no problem

443
00:24:46,080 --> 00:24:49,900
after passing through a hot shower

444
00:24:49,900 --> 00:24:56,580
Every day is no problem,
with a sleep pillow to restore your energy

445
00:24:59,720 --> 00:25:06,180
Every day is no problem,
I love a girl like me

446
00:25:06,180 --> 00:25:13,000
Every day is no problem,
Monday with hearts flying around

447
00:25:13,000 --> 00:25:17,160
Magic, no problem

448
00:25:20,320 --> 00:25:21,060
Dad

449
00:25:21,060 --> 00:25:22,980
What? Who are you?

450
00:25:22,980 --> 00:25:25,680
Aw, Dad, it's your son Kankichiro, isn't it?

451
00:25:25,680 --> 00:25:27,500
Son: No way, that's ridiculous

452
00:25:27,500 --> 00:25:29,940
But look, even our eyebrows are identical

453
00:25:29,940 --> 00:25:30,840
That's a lie

454
00:25:31,580 --> 00:25:33,660
Next time: Kankichiro's Summer

455
00:25:33,660 --> 00:25:34,480
Nice to meet you

456
00:25:34,480 --> 00:25:35,600
Don't you say that!

457
00:25:38,540 --> 00:25:40,640
Over there, there's Kameari

458
00:25:41,820 --> 00:25:43,960
Well, surely there's Kameari

459
00:25:45,220 --> 00:25:49,140
Everyone, come to our town!

460
00:25:50,080 --> 00:25:50,780
Thank you

